5. Vehicle is a category that has many other categories like trucks, scooters. Making Vehicle abstract
prevents anyone from instantiating a generic Vehicle object while still allowing it to serve as a
shared template and polymorphic reference type. but even though Vehicle cannot be instantiated directly
its subclasses inherit its private and protected fields therefore it needs a constructor so that they could
call super... as the first line of their own constructors to properly initialize those shared fields.

6. Composition is a strong "owns-a" relationship where the child object's lifecycle is strictly tied to the
parent object(vehicle and logbook). Aggregation is a weaker "has-a" relationship where objects can exist
independently of the container (depot and vehicle)

